0063 - dw_mmc: MMC_CAP_DONE_COMPLETE as a runtime knob, reads only by default
=============================================================================

Full copies of drivers/mmc/host/dw_mmc.c, dw_mmc.h and dw_mmc-pltfm.c from
linux-71-port (they include 0012, 0014 and 0039). Apply by copying over the
port tree's files.

What it does
------------
A 4 KiB swap-in on this board used to complete through THREE thread hops
after the card was done: the host's BH worker -> the mmc block layer's
complete_wq kworker -> blk_mq_raise_softirq from process context, which
wakes ksoftirqd -> the faulting task. MMC_CAP_DONE_COMPLETE lets the block
layer complete the request inside mmc_request_done(), in the BH, deleting
the middle hops. No host in the tree sets it; ours sets it per request from
dw_mci_request() when the request is a READ (mode 2), or always (mode 1),
or never (0):

    /sys/module/dw_mmc_pltfm/parameters/done_complete   (0644, default 2)

Writes keep the stock path on purpose: with the cap a write skips
mmc_blk_card_busy()'s CMD13 poll, so the card's program time would be
absorbed by dw_mci_wait_while_busy()'s atomic spin in the NEXT issue and
R1 error bits would go unreported (docs/sd-paging-programme-2026-09-24.md,
B1 ship gate). Queue depth is 1, so the cap seen at completion is the one
set at issue.

Measured 2026-09-24 (rootfs/sdlat 4 KiB random n=300, none scheduler,
same boot, /proc/stat ctxt per request):

    kernel #368  mode 0: min 1.34/1.33  p50 1.47/1.48  ctxt 4
                 mode 1: min 0.93/0.93/1.16  p50 1.42/1.44/1.27  ctxt 1-2
    kernel #369  mode 0: min 1.32  p50 1.60  p99 8.5   ctxt 3
                 mode 2: min 1.17/1.17  p50 1.28/1.28  p99 3.0/9.0  ctxt 2
    write check (mode 2): 24 MB O_DIRECT write, drop_caches, sha256 of the
    read-back MATCH, sdprobe busy waited 0, no dmesg errors.

The min is the per-request path with nothing else running; the p50 gain
is what a lone faulter sees. The timedemo gain is ~1% (2,329 faults x
~0.3 ms in 90 s) and is not measurable against the boot lottery - this is
a latency and hitch change, claimed from sdlat and ctxt only.

Also in this set: dw_mci_set_cap() helper (dw_mmc.c), the mode variable,
and the per-request hook at the top of dw_mci_request().
